 goes through shock  denial anger bargaining all the way down  to stage seven the last stage of  acceptance of being able to look in the  mirror  and accept yourself for everything that  you are knowing that everything that's  happened to you in your life has  happened for a reason  and and you know makes you into the  beautiful messy puzzle pieces that we  show up as every day  i feel like you're gonna help so many  people with  this album does that make you emotional  at all  thank you for saying that um no that's  exactly what i want to do  i i feel that music has the power to  heal  and it's that universal language to  bring us all together and and to connect  us  and um and so i really do hope these  songs can be support or empathy if  people are looking for that  or i really hope it inspires them to  sort of start their own  transformational journey to finding that  deeper level  of themselves because it's always within  us and and we're constantly transforming  and evolving as  as we go through life you know and as  things happen and  even through this global pandemic i mean  we're having to  ask a lot of questions and and you know  work on a lot of areas in our lives and  i know talking to a lot of my friends i  mean the past few months have been  have been big periods of transformation  where you're  where you're wondering okay how am i  doing my job how could i do my job more  efficiently  you know what are the small group of  friends that i really want to connect  with  or am i putting enough time into my  family like am i prioritizing the right  things in my life and so um  yes i really hope this album has has  legs and arms that um can inspire and  help a lot of people  were you opened up about your experience  as a sexual violence survivor  [Music]  mirror used to look so  innocent but that was all gone yesterday  what has the response been like for you  after sharing such a personal experience  like that  i had never talked about my story as a  little girl because i never wanted it to  be  about a publicity sense but i went to um  this place called youth for tomorrow  three years ago they're an organization  in the states that deal with kids who  have  gotten into the wrong situations or  youth specifically  12 to 18 who have been victims of sex  trafficking and rape  and i went there to help them launch  their music program three years ago and  i ended up sitting down at a conference  table with 12 other little girls  and i told them my story and i heard  their story and  they're things that are just so horrific  and so  i left that campus that day and was like  all right if i don't share my story  right now  then i'm holding back the opportunity to  help other little girls like that  or little boys like that or grown adults  because i feel like  it truly this happens far more in our  communities and our cities and our  towns more than we want to admit and um  and i just feel like the the  only way to  to to heal to help people heal is by  using our voices  and by by standing up and and saying  what we believe in  and you know if i would have had  somebody to hold little 13 year old  lindsay's hand  or 21 year old lindsay's hand and tell  her it was gonna be okay i feel like i  would have healed so much  faster so i decided to write a song  about it it's called make you  the cracks will heal which you'll always  feel the break  and that's what's gonna make you  i wrote it with brandy clark on this  album and um and i was able to launch my  own foundation as well  it's called the makey movement and the  foundation focuses on disenfranchised  youth specifically survivors  of sexual violence and domestic abuse  and i  truly just want other survivors to know  that they are not alone  and we can lean on each other just as my  female artist friends we can lean on  each other as survivors and  and know that that we're working through  this together you know it's one thing to  put something so personal into your art  to help other people heal too but then  to also release this song on global  forgiveness day i feel like  is so significant for so many reasons  how long did it take you and when did  you get to that point where you  were ready to forgive  you know i um from the first occurrence  when i was 13 i didn't tell my parents  for seven years  and um and those seven years were  were pretty heavy to be honest um  but i i forgave him  before i even told my parents and i  think that's maybe why i told my parents  as i finally got to that that place of  forgiveness  um you know obviously as a survivor it's  different in absolutely every case  and i think the the main  level of forgiveness is forgiveness of  yourself it is one thing to forgive  people in our lives who you know in in  various circumstances may have  have done things right or wrong but to  forgive ourselves  is truly where i feel the deepest level  of healing  lies because um we just carry so much  shame  and guilt and blame for things that  aren't our fault  or even are our fault but we we can't  carry that with us for the rest of our  lives because that's such a heavy weight  to carry  and so i feel like by talking about  things  it normalizes that shame and it brings  it  right here to the point where you can be  like okay this is what we're dealing  with  and when you can do that you feel  a freedom that is hard to even explain  i mean you feel like you can greek  deeper and you can wake up different  in in the morning and um and that's what  i want  to help other survivors feel this album  is the  is the seven stages of grief where are  you where are you at now how is your  heart now  my heart is good the the last song on  the record is ready to love  and i fully feel that i fully feel in  the place of acceptance and i feel that  acceptance is not  only being able to accept our past but  being able to open yourself up to new  things  and i truly feel open my heart is  um in the place where i'm just ready to  to  release this music and i'm also ready to  accept  love in ways that i i haven't been you  know  before what kind of energy do we want to  attract what kind of  love are we ready for  oh my gosh this is a great question we  want to attract  just creative and and connected  and open and  and exciting love i just want all of it
 

